# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
*.venv/

# Pytest
.pytest_cache/

# Data caches
/data/tile_cache/
/data/.partition_cache/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/

# Logs (run artifacts, never tracked)
*.log
nohup.out

# Data is re-fetched from the pinned HF dataset / GSI tiles — never tracked
# (tiles are licensed and not redistributed; see the data availability note)
# Leading slash anchors this to the repo root: unanchored "data/" also matched
# src/hflsim/data/, so editing the loader tripped "paths are ignored" on every
# `git add` even though the file was tracked.
/data/

# ResNet feature caches: rebuilt automatically (and validated against the
# dataset) by compute_feature_cache; at subsample 1.0 they exceed GitHub's
# 100 MB file limit, so the VM's auto-commit must never stage them.
img_features.npy

# Working notes. Kept locally, never tracked: they are drafts and scratch
# reasoning, not results, and a public repo should carry the evidence rather
# than the deliberation. PREREGISTRATION.md at the root IS tracked — it is the
# audit trail and belongs with the results it adjudicates.
REPORTS/

# Paper workspace. The manuscript and its rendered figures are the deliverable,
# not the artifact this repo exists to provide: the repo holds the code,
# configs, results and pre-registration that let someone reproduce and check the
# numbers. Keeping the manuscript out also means a draft in progress is never
# published by an ordinary `git push`.
main.tex
ref.bib
Figures/
scripts/paper_figures.py
scripts/system_figures.py

# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.lof
*.lot
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
main.pdf
